    {
      "id": "wp_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -264
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Wallpaper groups\n\nThe Symmetry node in `wallpaper` mode repeats a motif by one of the 17 plane symmetry groups — here p6m: six-fold turns and mirrors on a hexagonal lattice of `cell`-wide cells. The motif, two petals and a dot drawn near the origin, turns slowly, so the whole pattern breathes.\n\nPick another `group` (p4g, pgg, p31m …) to see the same motif obey a different symmetry.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 200
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Wallpaper groups\n\nThe Symmetry node in `wallpaper` mode repeats a motif by one of the 17 plane symmetry groups — here p6m: six-fold turns and mirrors on a hexagonal lattice of `cell`-wide cells. The motif, two petals and a dot drawn near the origin, turns slowly, so the whole pattern breathes.\n\nPick another `group` (p4g, pgg, p31m …) to see the same motif obey a different symmetry.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 200
      }
    },
